  "sourceLocator": {
    "chapter": "Rules Glossary",
    "section": "8.130",
    "heading": "Simultaneous Effects",
    "lineStart": 13645,
    "lineEnd": 13647
  },
  "section": "8.130",
  "rulesText": "If two or more things happen at the same time on a turn, the person at the game table - player or GM - whose turn it is decides the order in which those things happen. For example, if two effects occur at the start of a player character's turn, the player decides which of the effects happens first."
}
